  "reason": "Evidence: The top two experiments (config_045 at 0.725, config_007 at 0.721) both use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation, with weighted fusion slightly ahead. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs scgpt) is the dominant performance driver (~20-point gap), and imagenet_vit_l outperforms resnet50. However, aggregation method has only been tested as 'transformer' with the best RNA encoder. Question: Does avgpool aggregation with the proven-best components (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion) match or exceed transformer aggregation? This isolates the aggregation variable while holding all other factors at their empirically best settings. Why this is the best use: With only 3 experiments remaining, testing the single unexplored dimension (aggregation) around the current best configuration is the highest-information experiment. If avgpool performs comparably, it confirms the current best is near-optimal; if it underperforms, it confirms transformer is the right choice and we can focus remaining budget on other refinements. config_003 is the most targeted single-variable test from the current best."
